Z||000000||Dumba$$||12-18-2001||11:50 AM||||what is it <BR>currently i have aftermarket 15inch rims and i running 215-60-15's  they look ok but there huge<BR> and it pisses me off that my speedo is 10 mph off (i dont know how you guys with big wheels can stand that?) <BR>so ln a few months (hopefully) i will get some new tires <BR>what should i get?<BR>i want close to the factory size (height) so the speedo isnt off but i would like a little wider probibly<BR>please help<BR>thanks <P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Aura||12-18-2001||11:59 AM||||Change your Speed sensor gear on your tranny to one that came out of a 86-88 GT that came stock with that tire size. If it is a GT, then there is a problem elsewhere, most likely electronic, the speedo in my GT was alwys off about 15 KM... I just replaced it and everything seems to be fine now.<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips, Cross Drilled Rotors||||reg||1
